==Strategy==
Though the enemy backliners are certainly more dangerous, the Traitless threats comprise the main pushing force, and none of them spawn indefinitely. As such, the objective of this stage is to outlast the onslaught, then pick off the rangers.

It is recommended to start the stage as far away from your base as possible, use the first Gory and kill it with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] or a [[Talents|talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and immediately start rushing the enemy down. Don't worry if you hit the base too early, since only Mega Baa Baas spawn upon initial base hit. By now, the first dragon will have likely spawned. Use Can Can and BTrain to deal heavy damage to it before support arrives.

The stage is separated into three phases, a Rain D. phase, R. Ost phase, and finally a Master A. phase. This is the order in which you'll likely kill the enemies. The Master A. will naturally take the longest to kill, due to its high range along with DPS. You'll be chipping at him with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] for majority of the fight. As for the other enemies, Rain D. will be a nuisance on your front lines, but if you brought ample support, he shouldn't pose much of a threat. The strongest pusher in the stage is R. Ost, who spawns very late compared to the others, and will most likely be the reason you lose. Cyberpunk should be able to subdue his pushing power while units like Hitman melts him down. Don't worry if he pushes into your first Cyberpunk, that one wasn't meant to last very long anyways.

After Rain D. and R. Ost die, you'll have to play the long game chipping down Master A. while maintaining your cash. Cash isn't an issue in the previous parts of the stage, but will become a serious issue during the cleanup phase, where the cash bags of the stage start slowing in spawn rates. However, you're very unlikely to lose if you've reached this point, so just meatshield and chip away at Master A. with your units.

Bringing knockback units like [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] may prove to be more harm than good in this stage, as they can lead to your front lines pushing into the dragons' or Master A's range, resulting in a pushback or even outright defeat.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - With very high speed, the Extra Money ability and good damage, Bullet Train sees great utility. It can instantly kill Gory at level 42+ to dramatically boost income and can also help with chipping down the Dragons or Master A.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Stone's massive health makes it an excellent line of defense against the Traitless threats for its brief lifetime of ~1.3 seconds, particularly countering Mega Baa Baa by absorbing its three single-target Omni Strikes.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Hitman is a powerful LD specialist with Massive Damage to traitless. It can wipe out groups of Mega Baa Baas in one well-placed hit while tearing through R.Ost and Rain D. when given the chance. Hitman however does have a few weaknesses, namely its slow attack rate, blindspot, fragility and inability to outrange Rain D. or Master A.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - Cyberpunk retains its value from [[Draconian (Deadly)|Draconian]] with its chip damage at massive range, which is useful at any point in the fight. Though the Dragons' shields block status effects, Cyberpunk can still provide support by slowing the traitless enemies and delaying their advance, being one of the only options able to safely chip them and Master A.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - A great generalist meatshield despite his niche, Ramen's base stats are good enough for it to outperform even specialized anti-traitless meatshields, and is a viable pick here (only if boosted) despite there being no angels in this stage.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Strong rusher able take out large chunks of health from every enemy he hits. This can be useful to speed up the kills on R.Ost and Master A. in particular. He can be used to speed up the cleanup once the traitless enemies run out as well. He pairs well with a high levelled Thunderbolt cannon to guarantee hits, in addition to Stone Cat who can absorb Mega BaaBaa, preventing Bahamut from taking an unnecessarily damaging attack.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] - D'arktanyan is an LD rusher with Massive Damage against Traitless, low cooldown for an Uber, great health, very high speed, and 100% strengthen at 60% health. In cheese strategies he's the only option able to get around the Rain D and Mega Baa Baas, whereas for endurance battles he can easily best Hitman in action, able to even snipe Master A. with a stepping stone.
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Dusk]] - Since all of the pushers in the stage are traitless, Izanami can make disposing of them extremely easy. Her Conjure Spirit can also act like a Breakerblast + Thunderbolt, saving your units from certain death.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Hits hard and able to slow everything in place, he is amazing in this stage as his long range allows for him to hit even the dragons provided there is a stepping-stone. However, he is also risky here as he has a tendency to rush into the dragons' range, which can result in his death. If you decide to bring him, make sure you only send him out when there is an enemy in front of the dragons (preferably R.Ost).
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - A great crowd-controller for this stage, able to weaken both Aku and Traitless alongside good damage and amazing bulk. She can also pierce Malevolent King Dragon's shields with her [[Explosion|Explosions]]. She is also fairly refreshable with a cheap cost and fast cooldown.
*[[Supernova Cosmo]] - An obvious pick for this stage, as he outranges every enemy here. His attacks can one-shot the Gories and Mega Baa Baas, boosting your team's finance while crippling the dragons and the Traitless threats. He can also clear the way for Bahablast to land devastating hits on the main pushers.


